// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// `persistenceStrategy:` on a DataQualityValidation. Same category as
// ./no-registered-island-processor.pure and a cleaner example of it: nothing implements
// IDataQualityGrammarParserExtension, so getExtraDataQualityPersistenceStrategyParsers()
// returns emptyList and parseIsland's orElseThrow fires for every island type. Against the
// runner's jars the grammar refuses it earlier still.
//
// Pinned because "no processor is registered" is indistinguishable, from the outside, from
// "this construct is invalid" -- and from "the extension is not on your classpath". Three
// causes, one symptom. legend-lite has to decide deliberately which it is implementing.
###DataQualityValidation
DataQualityValidation fixture::neg::WithStrategy
{
   context: fromMappingAndRuntime(fixture::neg::M, fixture::neg::R);
   validationTree: $[ fixture::neg::Person { name } ]$;
   persistenceStrategy: Relational { };
}
